# Keep the developer's working tree out of the image.
#
# Without this, `COPY consumet/ ./consumet/` copied the LOCAL dist/ into the image. Combined with the
# old `npx tsc || true`, a build whose compile failed still shipped — running whatever dist/ happened
# to be lying around on the machine that built it. That is precisely the "stale dist/ with nobody
# noticing" failure H2 is about, so the build must always compile its own dist/ from the copied src/.
# node_modules is excluded for the same reason (host-arch native binaries + a stale tree): the build
# runs its own `pnpm install` in both consumet/ and api/. Lockfiles and package.json are NOT ignored.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build

.git
.gitignore
*.log
